# The build stage copies explicit paths rather than `COPY . .`, so nothing here
# is load-bearing for what ends up in the image. It is about the build *context*:
# every file not excluded is sent to the daemon before the first instruction
# runs, and an unignored node_modules is most of the build time on its own.
#
# It is also defence in depth. If a later change reaches for `COPY . .`, the
# secrets and the local build output are already out of reach.

node_modules
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github

# .env holds real credentials; .env.example is the checked-in template and is
# harmless, though nothing copies it either.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# Regenerated by `prisma generate` inside the build stage. Copying a host build
# in would risk a client generated against a different schema than the one the
# image ships.
src/generated

# Neither tier runs in the image.
test
scripts
jest.config.ts
tsconfig.test.json
